<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3152-JOIN-TIMEOUT-DUPLICATE-IDIOM>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3152-JOIN-TIMEOUT-DUPLICATE-IDIOM" ;
  triage:title "New bounded join-with-timeout primitive (admission.rs) duplicates a pre-existing sibling implementation (active_connection_registry.rs), a third variant in https_transport.rs" ;
  triage:description "M5-ADMISSION-FIX-3 introduces join_workers_with_timeout (crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport/admission.rs:29-60) with its own LOCAL_WORKER_JOIN_DEADLINE = 250ms constant. This duplicates, near-verbatim, the pre-existing join_dispatch_handle_with_timeout (crates/atm-daemon/src/active_connection_registry.rs:272-293), which already implements the identical recv_timeout-then-join-or-detach algorithm and is driven by TRACKED_DISPATCH_JOIN_DEADLINE = 250ms (same value, declared in the same file local_ipc_transport.rs:64). https_transport.rs's join_tracked_dispatches/HTTPS_TIMEOUT (~line 412, 5s deadline) is a third variant of the same pattern. This is the same duplicated-idiom anti-pattern QA-2 already caught once in this fix chain (admission-retry idiom, since correctly extracted into admission.rs's send_with_bounded_admission), now recurring in a new subsystem within the same round. Flagged by ruthless-boundary-qa as RBQA-F004 (critical) during M5-ADMISSION-QA-3. Recommend collapsing to one shared primitive (parameterize on completion-channel + join-handle + timeout + messages) consumed by all three call sites, or at minimum delete the duplicate LOCAL_WORKER_JOIN_DEADLINE constant and reuse TRACKED_DISPATCH_JOIN_DEADLINE." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "Architecture" ;
  triage:severity "Important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-02T21:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S13 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-02T21:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3152-JOIN-TIMEOUT-DUPLICATE-IDIOM/OCC-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3152-JOIN-TIMEOUT-DUPLICATE-IDIOM/OCC-2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3152-JOIN-TIMEOUT-DUPLICATE-IDIOM/OCC-3> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-02T22:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:progressNote "Initial triage pass: All three timeout-based join implementations exhibit identical pattern (recv_timeout + join_or_detach on success). Recommended action: Extract a shared primitive join_with_timeout_impl<T>(completion_rx, join_handle, timeout, subsystem, message) that can be reused by admission.rs, active_connection_registry.rs, and https_transport.rs. This unifies 250ms deadline pattern across two subsystems (LOCAL and TRACKED dispatch handlers) and clarifies the https_transport.rs 5s exception. Related to AI3152-JOIN-UNBOUNDED-RECUR; if that finding's 3 new unbounded joins are fixed by reusing the new primitive, both findings should be resolved together." ;
  triage:progressNote "M5-ADMISSION-QA-4 (commit 3f200470): fixed. arch-ctm's M5-ADMISSION-FIX-4 collapsed all three duplicated join-with-timeout implementations into one shared primitive, crate::daemon_worker_join::join_with_timeout (crates/atm-daemon/src/daemon_worker_join.rs). admission.rs's join_workers_with_timeout is gone (the whole admission.rs file was removed, folded into daemon_worker_join.rs). active_connection_registry.rs's join_dispatch_handle_with_timeout (still present, ~line 272-293) now delegates internally to daemon_worker_join::join_with_timeout instead of implementing its own recv_timeout-then-join loop. https_transport.rs's join_tracked_dispatches (still calling into active_connection_registry.rs's join_dispatch_handle_with_timeout at line 216, which itself calls join_with_timeout at line 276) also routes through the same shared primitive. Confirmed via direct read of all three call sites plus daemon_worker_join.rs. Only one underlying join-with-timeout mechanism remains; LOCAL_WORKER_JOIN_DEADLINE (250ms), TRACKED_DISPATCH_JOIN_DEADLINE (250ms), and HTTPS_TIMEOUT (5s) now remain solely as distinct timeout *values* passed as parameters to the shared primitive, not separate *implementations* -- the duplicated-idiom anti-pattern is resolved. Reviewer dispatch (req-qa/arch-qa/ruthless-boundary-qa) was unavailable this round due to a session-wide subagent spawn-limit (200/200); this verification is quality-mgr direct-read only -- flagged to team-lead in the QA-4 verdict." ;
  triage:progressNote "M5-ADMISSION-POSTMERGE-REVIEWERBACKED (integrate/phase-ai-31-33 @ c9ba04d9): reconfirmed fixed post-merge. Reviewer-backed recheck (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa independently corroborating; rust-qa-agent test/fmt pass but killed before full clippy completion) plus quality-mgr direct git/grep verification found the fix intact on the merged commit, matching origin/integrate/phase-ai-31-33. No regression." .

